## 🧠 8 lessons to take from the book

1. Discipline beats motivation. Train consistently, even when you don't feel like it.
2. Preparation builds confidence. In high-pressure situations, practice becomes your advantage.
3. Stay calm under pressure. Don't allow fear to make decisions for you.
4. The team comes before the ego. Individual talent is powerful, but coordination makes it effective.
5. Take responsibility. Focus on what you can control instead of blaming circumstances.
6. Adapt quickly. When the original plan fails, assess the situation and find another way.
7. Courage is action despite fear. Being brave doesn't mean feeling no fear.
8. Service gives purpose to success. Your abilities become more meaningful when they help others.

These are practical takeaways drawn from the book's accounts of military operations and service, rather than quotations from the author.

