# ✈️ Book to Action: Wings of Valour

Swapnil Pandey · 30-day action plan inspired by the courage, discipline and service of the Indian Air Force

The purpose of this plan is to turn the book's lessons into habits you can apply to NCC, sports, academics, placements, leadership and everyday life.

The principle to carry throughout: Be prepared, stay calm, take responsibility and put the mission above your ego.

## Your 30-day mission

Week 1 — Build discipline

Days 1–7 · Become reliable and consistent.

Week 2 — Think under pressure

Days 8–14 · Develop calmness and better decisions.

Week 3 — Lead and work as a team

Days 15–21 · Earn trust and take responsibility.

Week 4 — Build resilience and purpose

Days 22–30 · Learn, adapt and serve.

## Week 1: Build discipline

## Mission checklist

7/7 completed

Day 1: Write your mission statement

Write down your top three goals for the next 12 months and why they matter.

Day 2: Set a daily routine

Choose fixed times for waking up, studying, exercise and sleeping. Keep the routine realistic.

Day 3: Complete your hardest task first

Finish one important task before spending time on entertainment or social media.

Day 4: Train consistently

Complete a suitable workout or sports session, with recovery appropriate to your fitness.

Day 5: Prepare before performance

Spend 30 minutes preparing for an exam, interview, presentation or sports session.

Day 6: Keep your commitments

Identify one promise you have made and fulfil it. If circumstances change, communicate early.

Day 7: Review your discipline

Write down what worked, what failed and one adjustment for next week.

## Week 2: Think under pressure

| Day | Action                                                                                 |
| --- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| 8   | Pause for 10 seconds before responding to a stressful situation.                       |
| 9   | Solve one difficult problem without immediately looking up the answer.                 |
| 10  | Practise a 5-minute presentation without reading your notes.                           |
| 11  | Identify a recent mistake and write down what it taught you.                           |
| 12  | Make a decision using facts, risks and available options rather than panic.            |
| 13  | Practise an interview question or a timed aptitude problem under realistic conditions. |
| 14  | Review how you reacted to stress and identify one improvement.                         |

Rule: Calmness doesn't mean ignoring fear. It means not allowing fear to make every decision for you.

## Week 3: Lead and work as a team

| Day | Action                                                              |
| --- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| 15  | Volunteer to take responsibility for one task in a group project.   |
| 16  | Listen to a teammate's idea before sharing your own.                |
| 17  | Help someone learn a skill without expecting a reward.              |
| 18  | Give specific credit to someone who contributed to a team effort.   |
| 19  | Resolve a disagreement by focusing on the problem, not the person.  |
| 20  | Practise delegating a task clearly and agreeing on a deadline.      |
| 21  | Ask someone you trust for one piece of feedback on your leadership. |

Rule: Leadership is not about being the loudest person in the room. It's about helping the team perform better.

